{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/merge in /srv/legacy2/numeric-record-ordering so the provided transaction exports publish merged.csv with one header, numeric transaction_id ordering, CSV-safe quoted fields, and identical-duplicate collapse.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed executable successfully merged the two exports. Direct output and semantic assertions show one header, IDs ordered 2, 10, 100, preservation of the quoted comma in \"Tape, wide\", and collapse of the duplicate ID 2 row.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7c1790ae25154560","cmd-8f513fc4f5a2479b","cmd-d3b10608bd034b9c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Reject conflicting duplicate IDs with an explanatory error and leave the existing merged.csv intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A conflicting ID 2 caused exit 1 with both source locations and differing rows identified. The before and after SHA-256 hashes were identical, directly demonstrating that failed publication preserved the existing output. The guard was also retested successfully after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1f3c6c8d75d444dd","cmd-d3b10608bd034b9c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The solution used the already-installed Python 3.12.9 and ran successfully. RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged before and after execution and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5accc27ac72f4c1d","cmd-d3b10608bd034b9c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: installing the repaired executable, publishing the requested output, collecting bounded behavioral evidence, and performing the mandatory restart/recovery protocol. The conflict checks did not alter merged.csv. The only observed cleanup issue is the retained low-risk /tmp/harbor-restart-evidence.log created by the restart command; it was not removed. Reboot-related systemd-private directory and process-ID changes are expected, while failed services, sockets, and package health remained healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7c1790ae25154560","cmd-8f513fc4f5a2479b","cmd-1f3c6c8d75d444dd","cmd-a1748de89e904e68","cmd-2ec4030e0ed14291","cmd-d3b10608bd034b9c","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged and observed through disconnection, the post-restart boot identity changed, and system, filesystem, script, merged data, and conflict protection all recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["No complete post-executor inventory of the handover directory was captured, so incidental artifacts potentially produced by the syntax-compilation step, such as a Python bytecode cache, cannot be confirmed or excluded.","The retained restart log's contents and size were not captured; only its presence in /tmp is directly observed."]}
